# Project Conventions

## 1. Responsive & aligned on all devices

Follow the dedicated always-on rule **`responsive-ui.mdc`** (VIEWPORTS, no page overflow, `min-w-0`, logical props, mobile-first). Do not ship desktop-only layouts that merely shrink on mobile.

## 2. Import alias: use `~`

- Import from `~/...` (maps to `src/`).
- Never use deep relative imports like `../../components/...`.
- Same-folder relatives (`./button`) are OK inside a feature/ui folder.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
import { Button } from "../../components/ui/button";

// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from "~/components/ui";
```

`@/` is kept only for shadcn tooling compatibility; prefer `~/` in app code.

## 3. Barrel `index.ts` / `index.tsx` per folder

- Each components/screens/features/hooks/lib folder must expose a public API via `index.ts` (or `index.tsx` if needed).
- Import from the folder barrel, not deep file paths, when consuming outside that folder.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
import { SiteHeader } from "~/components/layout/site-header";

// ✅ GOOD
import { SiteHeader } from "~/components/layout";
```

## 4. Always use Yarn

- Package manager is **yarn** only.
- Do not use pnpm or npm for install/scripts in this repo.
- Examples: `yarn install`, `yarn dev`, `yarn build`, `yarn test`.

## 5. Keep useful package.json scripts

Maintain at least: `dev`, `build`, `start`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `format`, `format:check`, `test`, `test:watch`, `test:e2e`, and related helpers.